  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a poster, I want to reinsert an image I uploaded before, so that I do not upload it twice.\n\n### Scope\n\nHistory list with reinsert; 'remove' clears the local entry and says plainly that the image stays online (user feedback, ≈14 messages). Store from LOT-064 'histories' (if E-5 does not include rehost history, add it to LOT-064 first).\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: easy · Priority: low · post-MVP\n- Implements: FEAT-019 (#163)\n- Absorbs: FEAT-019 (local part only: server-side delete is not evidenced, HFR-PROTOCOL §7b B12)\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `ReplyService.swift` (`RehostUploadHistoryStore`)\n- Spec: `docs/features/FEAT-019.md` (feature spec, ADR 0011 §2; write it first if absent, crediting Bybifok) plus a short `docs/lots/LOT-103-*.md` pointing to it\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-102 (#193, done)\n- LOT-064 (#89, done)\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged\n\n### Feature umbrella\n\n- Implements FEAT-019 (#163), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: none; **this lot is the last one: its PR also says `Closes #163`**.\n\nFEAT issues (#145–#165) are umbrellas and are never claimed: claim this lot's issue; the PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #<FEAT issue>`.\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none known; any page state the spec needs and the fixtures lack is listed as *pending capture*, never hand-built (LESSONS 35-36)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Removal text states the image stays public on the host.\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
